{"operations":[{"content":"def is_valid_isbn10(isbn):\n    \"\"\"Check if the given string is a valid ISBN-10.\n\n    An ISBN-10 is valid if it consists of 10 characters, where the first 9 are digits,\n    and the last one is either a digit or 'X' (which represents 10).\n    The checksum is computed by multiplying each digit by its position (1 to 10) and\n    summing these products. The sum must be divisible by 11.\n\n    Args:\n        isbn (str): The ISBN-10 string to validate.\n\n    Returns:\n        bool: True if valid, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Remove hyphens and spaces\n    isbn = isbn.replace('-', '').replace(' ', '')\n\n    if len(isbn) != 10:\n        return False\n\n    total = 0\n    for i in range(9):\n        if not isbn[i].isdigit():\n            return False\n        total += (i + 1) * int(isbn[i])\n\n    # Check last character\n    if isbn[9] == 'X':\n        total += 10 * 10\n    elif isbn[9].isdigit():\n        total += 10 * int(isbn[9])\n    else:\n        return False\n\n    return total % 11 == 0\n","expected_sha256":"114aa799811c51f89a8ba9fc5692b4e682023d46a66fa224e724a76b75c28e58","kind":"modify","path":"src/isbn.py"}],"rationale":"Fixed is_valid_isbn10 to correctly handle 'X' as the check digit representing 10, preserving the public API and existing tests."}